From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:33:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] arm64: dts: apple: t600x: Report the GPU to the PMP
 while its driver is bound

Add the GPU's PMP report entry (report bit 9, PMGR device GFX) on t6000
and t6001, following the GPU driver rather than as its power domain:
reported before the GPU firmware has booted, it hangs t6001. With it, the
PMP raises the fabric and DRAM controller levels under GPU load and
lowers them again when the GPU idles.

Measured on an M1 Max (14") with the PMP running, GPU mat-vec
(4096x14336, f32/f16/bf16/q4_0) in GB/s: ~169/220/259/153 with the entry,
~163/190/188/136 without it, 168/217/237/148 with the PMP not running.
Idle power unchanged; about 10 W more under sustained GPU mat-vec, which
also runs 4-37% faster.

The id was checked against the t6000 (J314s) and t6001 (J314c) Apple
device trees. Not on t6002: the PMP has not been run on a two-die
machine yet.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6002.dtsi      |  3 +++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t600x-die0.dtsi | 13 +++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6002.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6002.dtsi
index 778d180a9..c60c62ab8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6002.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6002.dtsi
@@ -376,6 +376,9 @@ pmp_report_dispext3_die1: report@36 {
 	};
 };
 
+/* Not tested on t6002 (the PMP has not been run on a two-die machine). */
+/delete-node/ &pmp_report_gfx;
+
 &gpu {
 	compatible = "apple,agx-t6002", "apple,agx-g13d", "apple,agx-g13s";
 };
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t600x-die0.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t600x-die0.dtsi
index 6aea1407f..a2effb385 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t600x-die0.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t600x-die0.dtsi
@@ -48,6 +48,19 @@ pmp_report: pmp_report@28e3c0000 {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <0>;
 
+		/*
+		 * The GPU (PMGR "GFX", id 10) is reported to the PMP only while
+		 * its driver is bound. As the GPU's power domain (t8112's way),
+		 * GFX would be reported before the GPU firmware boots, which
+		 * hangs t6001.
+		 */
+		pmp_report_gfx: report@9 {
+			compatible = "apple,t6000-pmp-v2-report-entry";
+			reg = <0x9>;
+			label = "pmp-gfx";
+			apple,report-while-bound = <&gpu>;
+		};
+
 		pmp_report_ane_sys: report@a {
 			compatible = "apple,t6000-pmp-v2-report-entry";
 			reg = <0xa>;
-- 
